# NorthNarrow JA3 fingerprint blocklist (Tappa 10 N8 / design §10 + §13 Q5).
#
# Loaded at agent boot from /etc/northnarrow/netflow-ja3-blocklist.v1 (the
# install.sh helper drops this file under /etc/northnarrow/ if missing).
# Consumed by NN-L-NET-003 (a TLS ClientHello whose JA3 or JA4 is in the
# list — Medium, recorded, never acted on: a fingerprint names a TLS stack,
# not a program; lot 275, R6 of the external review of 04/11). Operators
# extend / narrow via the /etc/northnarrow/netflow-ja3-blocklist.local
# overlay — same `+entry` add / `-entry` disable schema as fim-paths.local
# (Tappa 9 C7).
#
# Format: one entry per non-empty / non-comment line. Each entry is a JA3
# (the 32-character hex MD5 hash, Salesforce 2017 spec) or a JA4 (the
# 36-character `t13d1516h2_8daaf6152771_02713d6af862` form, FoxIO 2023; JA3
# alone is unstable for clients that permute their extensions, Chrome from
# 108). The parser normalises uppercase input to lowercase, so operators can
# paste vendor-exported fingerprints in either case. `#` starts a comment;
# blank lines ignored. NO `+` / `-` directives in v1 — those belong in the
# `.local` overlay only.
#
# Curation policy (Tappa 10 §10):
# - V1.0 ships EMPTY. Populating this file requires threat-intel curation
#   that is out of scope for the V1.0 deploy. Operators with EDR-vendor
#   fingerprint exports drop them into the `.local` overlay.
# - Rationale (per design §10): a shipped public-IoC JA3 list goes stale
#   fast (offensive tooling rotates ClientHello defaults to evade
#   signature-based detection, and false-positive risk is high — many
#   legitimate clients share JA3 hashes with malware that targets the same
#   TLS library / cipher-suite preference). Operators with their own feed
#   know which fingerprints are load-bearing for their environment.
# - The agent boots cleanly with an empty default.
#
# Lot 275 closed BUG-025 (external audit NET-009): the `tls_hello` sensor
# captures an outbound flow's ClientHello and the parse worker fingerprints
# it. Where the sensor does not attach, the boot says so (the `tls_hello`
# degradation) and NN-L-NET-003 cannot match there.
#
# See docs/design/TAPPA10_NETWORK_OBSERVABILITY_DESIGN.md §13 Q5 + §10 for
# the rationale.

# (empty default — operator populates via netflow-ja3-blocklist.local)
